    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Gunnar Henderson** (63.69) and **Heliot Ramos** (63.06). **Gunnar Henderson** faces Weathers in a matchup that, while traditionally unfavorable for left-handed bats, is mitigated by an 8% boost from his #2 spot in the order and, critically, a 2% lift derived from the pitcher's slow delivery, which creates a prime opportunity to exploit our scarcity in stolen bases. **Heliot Ramos** benefits from the highest projected ceiling of the day against Sasaki; the 5.30 xERA of the opposing starter provides an excellent environment for **Heliot Ramos** to capitalize on his +19% SP skill adjustment. Despite facing a daunting 2.60 xERA from McDonald, **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) remains a must-start; while the matchup suppresses his raw projection, his position in the heart of the order and positive dynamic platoon factors keep his efficiency well above the threshold required to protect our game caps.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Josh Jung** (48.40), who sat on the cusp of the lineup. While he offers reliable production, he was ultimately edged out by **Coby Mayo** (60.25). Although **Coby Mayo** is also contending with a left-handed matchup against Weathers, his high park adjustment (+16%) and the potential for a stolen base against the pitcher\u2019s rhythm outweighed the moderate floor provided by **Josh Jung**. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.38) occupies the UTIL slot, buoyed by a strong 0.384 xwOBA that signals he is hitting the ball hard enough to survive a matchup against Rasmussen. Managers should monitor **Nolan Schanuel** (51.34) closely; while he clears the 40-point floor, his lack of high-ceiling peripherals like speed makes him the most vulnerable to a benching if we need to optimize for defensive versatility or late-game pinch-hitting shifts. We remain cautious regarding **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to track as unavailable due to his IL designation, leaving a significant void in our outfield speed profile.",
